.\n\nOption D: People can generate electricity by talking or eating. Yes, the device uses talking or eating (chewing) to generate electricity. So D is consistent.\n\nSo the inconsistent one is B. Because the text describes the device as being used through jaw movement, not exercise. So B is wrong.\n</think>\n\nThe inconsistent option is **B**. The text explicitly states that the device generates electricity through ** jaw movement** when talking or eating, not through exercise. Option B incorrectly claims the method involves exercise, which contradicts the described application. \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}",
