es the \"trend of technological development,\" which is a secondary aspect but not the core focus.  \n- **B** directly addresses the critical challenge: prioritizing neither cost reduction at the expense of service or user safety. This aligns with the text's emphasis on maintaining \"full play\" of limited manpower and avoiding shortcuts like ignoring user needs.  \n- **C** and **D** mention \"user needs\" and \"better service quality,\" respectively. While these are important values, the text\u2019s core is not about adopting technologies based solely on user needs or prioritizing service quality over all else, but rather the practical necessity of balancing these factors.  \n\n**Correct Answer:**  \n\\boxed{B}",
