      "text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The problem is about a store that introduced some personalized products, and the manager thinks the increase in sales is because of those. We need to figure out which of the options best supports that view. \n\nFirst, let me restate the context to make sure I get it. The store has these new personalized products in a separate area. After three months, the manager says that compared to before the introduction, the total sales have increased a lot. So the manager thinks the main reason is the new products. The question is asking which of the options, if true, would support that view.\n\nSo the options are A, B, C, D. Let's go through each one.\n\nOption A: For three months, sales and sales of these personalized items have been limited. Hmm. If the personalized items' sales were limited, that might mean the manager is right. Because if they weren't selling well, the manager wouldn't have introduced them. But wait, the manager is claiming the increase is because of the new products. So if the new products' sales were limited, that would actually contradict the manager's point. Because if they weren't selling, why would the manager think the increase is due to them? So maybe A is not supporting the manager's view. Instead, it might be a reason why the manager thought the increase was because of the new products, but actually, maybe the other factors caused the increase. So A might not be the correct answer.\n\nOption B: It is mainly young people who come to the store to consume, and young people like to try new things. If the store is targeting young people who like new things, that could explain why the sales increased. Because introducing new products would fit with that customer base. So if the manager is of the view that the increase is due to new products, and the customer base is young people who try new things, that would support the manager's reasoning. So B seems like a strong supporter.\n\nOption C: In the past three mon