cientific basis for genetic foods, not on the causes of illness. This statement is a common misconception and not supported by the given information.\n\n- **D) Eating health products may not promote your health.**  \n  Since the problem explicitly states these products are not helpful and lacks scientific justification, eating them cannot promote health. This directly follows from the provided reasoning.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}",
