ntrasts two companies of the same scale: one with extensive international operations and the other with limited internationalization. If the profit of the latter is lower, this confirms that internationalization is a critical factor for success.  \n- **Option B** is true but irrelevant to the reason given (oil companies are not inherently less successful; it merely confirms oil companies\u2019 dominance, not Shell\u2019s specific success due to internationalization).  \n- **Option C** and **D** discuss broader trends (globalization and stable prices) that support efficiency but do not specifically address why Shell outperforms its competitors uniquely through internationalization.  \n\nThus, **A** provides the most direct, comparative evidence supporting the claim.  \n\n\\boxed{A}",
