t, which aligns with the context. So D is correct.\n\nSo going back, the incorrect statement is C. Because the context says practice is the only criterion, so there can't be other ones. Therefore, the answer should be C.\n</think>\n\nThe context states that **practice** is the **sole** criterion for testing truth, meaning no other methods are valid.  \n\n- **Option A** correctly affirms that practice can test truth.  \n- **Option B** mirrors the context by asserting practice is the sole method.  \n- **Option C** incorrectly claims other criteria exist, contradicting the context.  \n- **Option D** correctly states no other criteria exist.  \n\nThe incorrect answer is **C**.  \n\n\\boxed{C}",
