e main point. The tax rate is being adjusted to 25%, which is a moderate low internationally, and this will help in improving competitiveness. So D is the main content.\n\nWait, but let me check again. The options are about the main content of the passage. The passage is explaining why a 25% tax rate is appropriate: reducing domestic burden, controlling revenue loss, aligning with international standards. The options are about different aspects. The main idea is that the tax rate is set to 25% to address the domestic issue. So among the options, D says adjusting the tax rate will help improve competitiveness. The passage does mention that the new rate is internationally competitive, which is good for competitiveness. So D is correct. The other options are either talking about equal treatment (A), competition (B), or the tax rate's position (C). The main focus is on the policy's objective, which is stated early: \"to reduce the tax burden on domestic enterprises and to control the reduction in fiscal revenue within an affordable range, and to consider the tax rates of the international community, especially those of neighboring countries.\" So the main content is about the policy's goals, which is what D states: \"Adjusting the tax rate will help to improve the competitiveness of enterprises.\" Yes, because competitiveness is a reason given in the passage. So D is the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe main content of the passage revolves around the introduction of a new 25% enterprise income tax rate in China, designed to address several objectives: reducing the tax burden on domestic enterprises, controlling the reduction in fiscal revenue, aligning with international standards, and improving competitiveness relative to neighboring countries. Among the options provided:\n\n- **Option A** focuses on \"internal and external differences\" but the passage does not explicitly compare these, making it less relevant.  \n- **Option B** mentions \"competition on the same stag