ct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe letter argues that a budget increase alone doesn\u2019t justify the conclusion that the planning department now spends five times as much. To support this claim, the correct option must explain why the budget growth isn\u2019t proportionate to a fivefold increase relative to 2001\u2019s $100,000. \n\n- **Option A** (restructuring in 2003 broadened duties) directly addresses this: the increase could be due to expanded roles, not just original work. This explains why the ratio isn\u2019t fivefold.  \n- **Options B, C, D** discuss other factors (departmental changes, inflation, or budget fluctuations) but don\u2019t directly validate the letter\u2019s claim about the budget increase\u2019s rationalization.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}",
